# Task 156-003 Execution Plan

## Goal
Wire applyCascadeToSprint (NO_GO → cascade-block dependents) into runEvaluatePhase
and applyUnblockToSprint (DONE → unblock dependents) into runFixPhase. Both functions
are exported from sprint-spawner.ts but currently dangling (no runtime caller).
Emit two new aggregate events: BRAIN→*:DEPENDENCY_CASCADE_APPLIED + BRAIN→*:DEPENDENCY_UNBLOCK_APPLIED.

## Scope (filesWrite)
- src/orchestra/sprint-phases.ts (modify)
- tests/orchestra/cascade-unblock-wire.test.ts (new)

NOTE: event-stream.ts CHANNELS constant is OUT OF SCOPE — emit new channel codes via
string literals (writeEvent accepts arbitrary `channel: string`).

## Approach
1. Import writeEvent, getCurrentSprintId, applyCascadeToSprint, applyUnblockToSprint
   into sprint-phases.ts.
2. In runEvaluatePhase: after each task evaluated as NO_GO, build FailureContext
   from result + call applyCascadeToSprint. Also fire BRAIN→*:DEPENDENCY_CASCADE_APPLIED
   summary event with { failedTaskId, blockedTaskIds, decision }.
3. In runFixPhase: after each fix task evaluated DONE/GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT, call
   applyUnblockToSprint with the original (fixed) task id. Fire summary event
   BRAIN→*:DEPENDENCY_UNBLOCK_APPLIED with { resolvedTaskId, unblockedTaskIds }.
4. Persist task status mutations (PAUSED / PENDING) to .tasks/task-NNN.json so
   sprint-spawner reads see updates and Auditor dashboards reflect new state.
5. Wrap all calls in try/catch (fail-safe) — cascade/unblock failure must not
   break the evaluation pipeline.

## Test Plan (cascade-unblock-wire.test.ts)
- Test A: runEvaluatePhase NO_GO → 2 dependent tasks transition PENDING → PAUSED;
  BRAIN→*:DEPENDENCY_CASCADE_APPLIED event emitted with blockedTaskIds.
- Test B: runFixPhase DONE for fix task → 2 PAUSED dependents return to PENDING;
  BRAIN→*:DEPENDENCY_UNBLOCK_APPLIED event emitted with unblockedTaskIds.
- Test C: RUNTIME failure (no cascade) → no PAUSED transitions, no event.

## Verify
- npx tsc --noEmit
- npx vitest run tests/orchestra/cascade-unblock-wire.test.ts
